In commit "wallet: migration, make sqlite creation robust against failures" (b9486540d774f2e07ecce93af0637d6e685a93e0)

This duplicates the `backup_prefix` code in `MigrateLegacyToDescriptor`, which is nontrivial and IMO fragile. It would make more sense to move into a helper both places call so the logic is not duplicated and both call sites can be simpler. Here is a refactoring that can be applied with `git apply` on top of this commit, with no change in behavior:

<details><summary>diff</summary>
<p>

```diff
diff --git a/src/wallet/wallet.cpp b/src/wallet/wallet.cpp
index a40794237f5..8e21044bfb9 100644
--- a/src/wallet/wallet.cpp
